"""Why each case distractor fails; returned only after a learner submits."""
MISTAKES=[
('SDK objects couple every caller to changing vendor fields; normalize at one boundary.','Text existence does not establish completion, approval or durable save.'),
('Question-only keys omit owner and revision, allowing stale/cross-owner reuse.','History, instructions, tools and retries can consume input work beyond the visible reply.'),
('gather collects outcomes but does not limit simultaneous provider work.','A timed-out operation must release its permit or later requests can stall.'),
('Container/codec bytes are not raw signed16-bit samples; the declared wire format would be false.','An unbounded backlog increases memory and audible delay even while data continues to arrive.'),
('Already scheduled sound can play after generation stops; cancel playback too.','Replay can duplicate acknowledged work or corrupt a provider session; use its documented recovery boundary.'),
('Failed attempts still cost resources, and attempted requests are not accepted outputs.','First output does not measure the completed task or playback backlog.'),
('A received upload may fail extraction/indexing; activating early replaces usable evidence with broken state.','Digest equality identifies bytes, not another owner’s permission.'),
('The exception changes the rule, so separating it can produce an unsupported answer.','Word counts and provider tokenization are different units.'),
('Padding changes array length but does not align learned coordinate meanings.','Equal dimensions do not make different model spaces comparable.'),
('Unauthorized text has already crossed the retrieval boundary before citations are hidden.','A user/model field naming an owner is not authenticated server identity.'),
('Uncalibrated score scales can let one retriever dominate for arbitrary numerical reasons.','Duplicate IDs do not represent independent supporting evidence or votes.'),
('A reranker index refers to the original array position, not a source identity.','An out-of-range position cannot resolve to an authorized submitted candidate.'),
('Reference identity proves the page exists; the page may contradict the claim.','Fluent language is independent of factual support and applicability.'),
('The missing terminal event leaves an incomplete generation with unvalidated provenance.','Independent generation attempts are not guaranteed to continue the same draft or state.'),
('No-source queries have no positive passage-recall denominator; test their behavior separately.','Scoring only answered queries hides answerable questions missed by retrieval.'),
('The model cannot grant itself tenant identity or connector permission.','A lost response to a write can mean the effect already occurred; blindly retrying risks duplication.'),
('Process globals disappear on replacement and are not durable checkpoints.','A stale state version can consume approval twice or apply it to changed work.'),
('Approval must bind the actual destination and other effect fields; a label is insufficient.','Expired authority cannot authorize a later write, even for an unchanged payload.'),
('A summary does not override source revocation or membership changes.','A shorter key cannot justify cross-owner cache access.'),
('Shared sources and duplicated prompts do not provide independent verification.','Every branch consumes resources; ignoring slow/duplicate calls distorts the comparison.'),
('Discovery describes capability, while invocation still needs permission/schema checks.','Local execution does not grant the caller unrestricted filesystem access.'),
('A new key can create a second event when the original write already committed.','Timeout means the local caller lacks certainty, not that the destination rolled back.'),
('Acknowledging before commit can lose accepted work after a crash.','Delivery retries are the same logical event, not permission for another effect.'),
('Confidence in a draft does not establish current write authority or reviewed recipients.','A model assertion is not a trusted reviewer decision or connector grant.'),
('Valid references can still contradict the answer’s claims.','Low temperature does not remove model/judge error or version variability.'),
('IDs without inputs/expectations execute no meaningful behavior.','Sending labels to the executor leaks the answer and invalidates the evaluation.'),
('Aggregate gains cannot compensate for a mandatory authorization failure.','Changing prompts changes the candidate; otherwise the report cannot identify what was evaluated.'),
('Parallel durations overlap; summing them overstates wall time.','A useful trace needs identifiers/status/timing, not full private content by default.'),
('Removing failures drops real spend from the useful-output denominator.','Cheap rejected output can increase correction work and fail the quality floor.'),
('Completion and semantic review are separate;13 completed outputs remain unreviewed.','Unavailable attempts belong in reliability/accounting, not a hidden excluded population.'),
('db is container DNS, and exposing database credentials to browser code breaks the service boundary.','A running process can have an unavailable required dependency.'),
('A request limit cannot add GPU memory, provider quota or worker capacity.','Each replica would count a different local balance and overspend the shared allowance.'),
('Assumed memory arithmetic is not measured model/runtime throughput.','Similar HTTP shapes do not imply identical tokenization, capabilities or quality.'),
('Independent local allowances multiply the total admissions across replicas.','Fallback changes data processing location and quality; those constraints still apply.'),
('Moving local-only data violates the routing authorization even if quality improves.','Different datasets confound the route comparison with workload difficulty.'),
('Autoscaling configuration expresses a limit/intention rather than an observed load envelope.','Missing evidence stays a blocker; a checked UI box cannot supply the missing report.'),
]
assert len(MISTAKES)==36
BOUNDARY_MISTAKES=[
('An SDK return is not the application completion/validation boundary.','A nonempty fragment can be partial; content presence does not establish completion.'),
('Identical question text cannot make a changed source revision fresh.','TTL bounds age, but does not prove the underlying source or permission is unchanged.'),
('Keeping a timed-out permit can starve every later request.','Increasing capacity can violate the provider limit; cleanup should restore the original bound.'),
('The bounded queue accepted two frames and exposed three overflows; it did not retain all five.','A queue simulation says nothing about speaker recognition or model capability.'),
('Input capture settings do not cancel browser audio already scheduled for playback.','Token accounting does not stop an audio buffer; cancel the scheduled nodes.'),
('Frames are units of transport, not accepted user tasks.','Choosing only successful cheap attempts removes real spend from the workload.'),
('Owner permission cannot be inherited merely from equal file bytes.','Index activation also requires scope/revision/index checks; the digest does not supply them.'),
('Chunk count says nothing about preserving the rule and its exception.','Equal character length can cut a condition in half and uses a different unit from model tokens.'),
('Dimension compatibility is necessary but learned coordinate meanings can still differ.','Cosine operates on coordinates; it cannot align unrelated model spaces.'),
('Hiding an owner field after retrieving private text does not undo the disclosure.','A generator instruction cannot repair unauthorized retrieval that already happened.'),
('Fusion changes rank aggregation, not factual support of each result.','Authorization is checked before ranking; high rank cannot grant permission.'),
('Modulo mapping invents an unrelated candidate identity.','Provider array positions are not database document IDs.'),
('Citation membership passes on this contradiction; only claim/evidence review exposes the reversal.','Valid JSON proves structure, not whether the policy entails the claim.'),
('The last delta may be one word and lacks validated completion provenance.','Concatenation of partial fragments is still partial when the terminal event is absent.'),
('At least one hit is hit rate; one of two required passages gives recall0.5.','Recall uses labeled relevant passages, not every irrelevant document in the corpus.'),
('The model-controlled owner field cannot authenticate its caller.','A tool description is capability metadata and may itself be untrusted.'),
('A stable thread ID cannot recover a checkpoint that was never persisted.','External effects are not automatically rolled back when process-local graph memory disappears.'),
('The destination is an effect field; title equality does not preserve payload approval.','Login time is not the approval contract; changed content needs current exact review.'),
('Fluency does not restore revoked evidence authority.','A larger window increases capacity, not permission to use stale content.'),
('Independent parallel spans overlap; summing them double-counts their wall time.','Parallelism does not halve an individual branch duration; the slowest dependency still matters.'),
('A read-only policy tool does not expose an unrelated filesystem capability.','Successful initialization is not proof of safe future tool arguments or results.'),
('A lost acknowledgement leaves destination state unknown, so a new key risks duplication.','Sending a request is not evidence the remote system committed it.'),
('Repeated delivery is the same logical event and must not create a new operation.','A valid retry can be benign; discarding the original too loses accepted work.'),
('A read grant does not imply write authority.','Availability describes time occupancy, not consent to create or invite.'),
('Automation can be wrong; retain the reviewed disagreement and investigate.','Choosing the higher score selects the answer you prefer rather than calibrating evidence.'),
('Tenant variants share a mechanism/template; describe family and scope coverage separately.','Executing120 contract cases is not120 simultaneous requests or a capacity benchmark.'),
('A required isolation gate cannot be averaged away.','Removing a rare critical case hides the release risk instead of fixing it.'),
('Full documents are not needed for correlation and expand trace data exposure.','Raw exceptions may contain secrets or private payloads; stable categories are sufficient for public errors.'),
('List price omits retry spend and reviewer correction work.','The fastest success is a selected sample and ignores tails, failures and acceptance.'),
('Thirteen completed outputs lack review and seven attempts never completed.','Excluding unavailable attempts changes the reliability denominator and hides failures.'),
('Liveness and dependency readiness make different claims.','A cached browser result cannot prove the database is currently usable.'),
('Raising a configured request limit does not raise observed hardware/downstream capacity.','Rejected offered work belongs in the envelope report even if it was not completed.'),
('The worksheet supplies assumptions; p95 requires observed workloads and timing.','GPU/runtime/model/context choices materially change capacity, not just region.'),
('Separate local counters add their allowances; equal names do not synchronize them.','Local buckets do not cancel; each independently admits its burst.'),
('Model price cannot authorize processing restricted data elsewhere.','Removing a tenant label does not remove private document content or its residency restriction.'),
('Enabling autoscaling sets behavior/limits but measures no actual throughput.','Serverless platforms and providers still have concurrency, quota, time and hardware bounds.'),
]
assert len(BOUNDARY_MISTAKES)==36
